<title>BULGARIA: YIELD FALLS TO 3.77 PCT ON BULGARIA 4-WK T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>YIELD FALLS TO 3.77 PCT ON BULGARIA 4-WK T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yield fell on Bulgaria's Finance</p>
<p>Ministry four-week discount T-bills at the daily auction on</p>
<p>Monday as the issue was oversubscribed, a central bank official</p>
<p>said.</p>
<p>The average yield to maturity on the issue was 3.77 percent</p>
<p>against 3.81 percent on Thursday and Friday and 3.80 percent at</p>
<p>Wednesday's auction, said the official.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3037297002</p>
<p> Maturity			four weeks</p>
<p> Par value		     24,000 mln levs</p>
<p> Issue date		    June 3</p>
<p> Maturity date		 July 1</p>
<p> Bids received		 32,886 mln levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   96.36 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 24,000 mln levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  96.37 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     3.77 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
</text>
